{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Who executes the judgment of the orphan and the widow.</b> Even though He is exalted, as He said 'the great, the mighty, and the awesome El,' He nonetheless executes the judgment of the orphan and the widow. And this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: this matter is written in the Torah, repeated in the Prophets, and tripled in the Writings — in every place where you find the greatness of the Holy One, blessed be He, there you find His humility. And so David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 68:5-6): ״סלו לרוכב בערבות ביה שמו״, and immediately adjacent to it: ״אבי יתומים ודין אלמנות״. And so Isaiah, peace be upon him, said (Isaiah 57:15): ״שכן עד וקדוש שמו מרום וקדוש אשכן ואת דכא ושפל רוח״." "<b>And loves the stranger.</b> And since this is so, you too shall love the stranger; and so it is written in another place (Leviticus 19): ״ואהבת לו כמוך״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:17.619597724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}